  data: {
    LLM: "Priority is winning the first trick or setting the trump. Because it's a 32-card deck, counting cards is much easier and absolutely necessary.\n\nThe '9' and 'Jack' of trumps are the most powerful cards. If you hold both, you have a massive advantage and should bid aggressively.\n\nDefensive Play: If you are the Defender, your goal is to 'bust' the Declarer by winning just enough points to prevent them from hitting the majority. Force the Declarer to use their trumps on minor tricks.",
